---
import Accordion from '@/components/accordion.astro'
import AccordionItem from '@/components/accordion-item.astro'
---

<section class="bg-[#f3f3f3] px-5 py-32 lg:px-0" id="publications">
    <div class="container mx-auto flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2 class="text-center text-3xl font-semibold">Selected Publications</h2>
        <p>
            &lt;&lt; My work with colleagues explore three interrelated areas in management
            research. &gt;&gt;
        </p>
        <Accordion>
            <AccordionItem
                name="publications"
                icon="fa:paper-plane"
                title="Work - Family Boundary Management"
            >
                <p>
                    I explore and address questions on how work-family enrichment is achieved, how
                    employees can avoid conflict and what are best possible solutions to ensure
                    motivated employees across domains. Our research develops interesting concepts
                    such as “family crafting”, “integration”, “segmentation” and “relational
                    crafting”.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <strong>
                                <a
                                    target="_blank"
                                    href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001879119300375"
                                >
                                    Serving followers and family? A trickle-down model of how
                                    servant leadership shapes employee work performance
                                </a>{' '}
                            </strong>
                            Jakob Stollberger, Mireia Las Heras,&nbsp;Yasin Rofcanin, Maria Jose
                            Bosch Kreis – Journal of Vocational Behavior – February 2019
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <strong>
                                <a target="_blank" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27101338/">
                                    Family supportive supervisor behaviors and organizational
                                    culture: Effects on work engagement and performance
                                </a>{' '}
                                –&nbsp;
                            </strong>
                            Yasin Rofcanin, Mireia Las Heras , Arnold B Bakker – Journal of
                            occupational Health Psychology – April 2016
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </AccordionItem>
            <AccordionItem
                name="publications"
                icon="fa:paper-plane"
                title="Proactive Work Behaviours"
            >
                <p>
                    How can employees be proactive? What is the role of managers and organizations?
                    Are proactive work behaviours good or bad? In my recent papers, I develop and
                    implement these ideas.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <a
                                target="_blank"
                                href="https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0018726718779121"
                            >
                                <strong>
                                    Relational job crafting: Exploring the role of employee motives
                                    with a weekly diary study
                                </strong>
                            </a>{' '}
                            – Yasin Rofcanin, Arnold Bakker, Aykut Berber, Ismail Golgeci, Mireia
                            Las Heras – Human Relations – April 2019
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <a
                                target="_blank"
                                href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001879119301472"
                            >
                                <strong>
                                    Seeking an “i-deal” balance: Schedule-flexibility i-deals as
                                    mediating mechanisms between supervisor emotional support and
                                    employee work and home performance
                                </strong>
                            </a>{' '}
                            – Ciara M. Kelly,&nbsp;Yasin Rofcanin, Mireia Las Heras, Chidiebere
                            Ogbonnaya, Elise Marescaux, María José Bosch – Journal of Vocational
                            Behavior – April 2020
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <a
                                target="_blank"
                                href="https://researchportal.bath.ac.uk/en/publications/how-do-flexibility-i-deals-relate-to-work-performance-exploring-t"
                            >
                                <strong>
                                    How do flexibility i-deals relate to work performance? Exploring
                                    the roles of family performance and organizational context
                                </strong>
                            </a>{' '}
                            – Yasin Rofcanin, Mireia Las Heras, P. Matthijs Bal, Jakob Stollberger –
                            Journal of Organisational Behaivour – October 2017
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </AccordionItem>
            <AccordionItem
                name="publications"
                icon="fa:paper-plane"
                title="Individualization of HRM Practices"
            >
                <p>
                    Every employee is unique and has certain work needs and preferences. I develop
                    and explore the idea of differentiating human resource practices for
                    organizations.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <strong>
                                <a
                                    target="_blank"
                                    href="https://psycnet.apa.org/record/2017-24675-001"
                                >
                                    How do flexibility i‐deals relate to work performance? Exploring
                                    the roles of family performance and organizational context.
                                </a>{' '}
                                –&nbsp;
                            </strong>
                            Yasin Rofcanin, Aykut Berber, Elise Marescaux, Matthjis Bal,&nbsp;Farooq
                            Mughal, Mine Afacan Findikli – Human Resource Management Journal –
                            December 2018
                        </p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            <strong>
                                <a
                                    target="_blank"
                                    href="https://journals.aom.org/doi/10.5465/AMBPP.2018.38"
                                >
                                    Seeing Eye to Eye on Family Supportive Supervisor Behaviors: The
                                    Impact on Employee Outcomes
                                </a>{' '}
                                –&nbsp;
                            </strong>
                            Elise Marescaux,&nbsp;Yasin Rofcanin, Mireia Las Heras – Academy of
                            Management Best Paper Proceedings – July 2018
                        </p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </AccordionItem>
        </Accordion>
        <a
            class="font-semibold text-black italic transition-all hover:text-[#23a455]"
            target="_blank"
            href="https://researchportal.bath.ac.uk/en/persons/yasin-rofcanin"
        >
            &gt;&gt; Click here to see my all publications &lt;&lt;
        </a>
    </div>
</section>
